INTERPRETATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HYP-2028 survives the lift: every sector-vector gives a finite
   Gabor trienerment, so global existence is still not the obstruction.
2. The LRC target becomes sharper: not a favorite sector vector, but a
   marked zero column in the two-sector Gabor atom grid.
3. Runner trienerments and Gabor trienerments use ties oppositely:
   observer loneliness deletes real near-ties, while it creates a large
   unresolved zero block among observer-window Gabor atoms.
4. The bounded fixed-clock menus see only part of the global Gabor-class
   image, so the Gabor angle is useful only as a fixed-clock menu/fiber
   restriction, not as global realizability.
